  {
    id: "integrations",
    heading: "Integrating kintone, freee, Money Forward, Salesforce, LINE, Slack and Chatwork",
    paragraphs: [
      "A typical Japanese SME uses several cloud tools that do not talk to each other: kintone for customer or project records, freee or Money Forward Cloud for accounting and invoices, Chatwork or Slack for internal chat, Google Workspace or Microsoft 365 for email and files, and sometimes Salesforce or HubSpot for sales. Much of the value of custom software in Japan is simply connecting them, so information is entered once and trusted everywhere.",
      "<strong>Common patterns.</strong> A paid order in Shopify or your own system creates an invoice or journal entry in freee or Money Forward Cloud. A new kintone record appears in a customer portal, and changes made there flow back. A won deal in Salesforce generates a quotation PDF in the company's own layout. An overdue task posts a reminder to Chatwork. A booking confirmation, reminder or delivery update reaches the customer on LINE.",
      `<strong>LINE.</strong> LINE has more than 100 million monthly users in Japan according to LY Corporation, so many customer-facing systems send notifications through a LINE Official Account (${ja("LINE公式アカウント")}) and the Messaging API. LINE Notify, which many companies used for quick internal alerts, ended in March 2025, so older scripts that relied on it need moving to the Messaging API, Slack, Chatwork or Microsoft Teams. Message volume affects what your company pays LINE, so we design notifications to be useful rather than frequent.`,
      "<strong>Doing integrations properly.</strong> We use official APIs and webhooks rather than scraping screens. Each integration runs under a service account your company owns, with the narrowest permissions the job needs. Failed calls are retried safely without creating duplicate invoices, every sync is logged, and a person is alerted when something needs attention. When a SaaS vendor changes its API, maintenance covers the update.",
      `Where the integration is mainly about automating a human routine, such as reading orders, drafting replies or summarising meetings, the <a href="/japan/ai-automation-engineer/">AI automation engineer page for Japan</a> covers the AI side in more depth.`,
